the same as before.\n\n**CI:** passed on 08d3cd5986 (run ci-0001).", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-fin-212-bankers-rounding", "confidence": 0.93}, "confidence": 0.93}, {"t_ms": 378483, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01TWCegrPGhHcJDN6GJ6pnsX", "tool": "open_pr", "state": "VERIFIED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": ["postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-fin-212-bankers-rounding", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 378483, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01TWCegrPGhHcJDN6GJ6pnsX", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 382086, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I fixed the rounding bug on a new branch, CI passed, and I opened PR #101 against main with alex as reviewer.\n\n- **Cause:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` rounded half-cents up, even though its own comment says it uses banker's rounding (FIN-212). That's why `tests/test_money.py` failed.\n- **Fix:** On the branch `fix/fin-212-bankers-rounding`, I changed one line so it rounds half-cents to the nearest even cent. That's the only change.\n- **Effect:** Amounts that land exactly on a half-cent now round differently, for example 2.665 \u2192 2.66 instead of 2.67. All other amounts round the same as before.\n- **CI:** Passed on commit 08d3cd5986.\n- **PR:** https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101\n\nI didn't merge it, because merging into main needs a code owner's approval.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I'll start by looking at the repository and the relevant files.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01BXrtZSEVbh8N4hWdqNTwzc", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"confidence": 0.95}, "name": "list_files", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01PJNg